### 1. Check Server Status
GET http://localhost:5000/
Accept: application/json

### 2. Register a New Student
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "John",
  "last_name": "Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "student"
}

### 3. Login
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

> {% 
    client.global.set("auth_token", response.body.token); 
%}

### 4. Get Current User Profile (Requires Token from Login)
# Note: If you are not using a tool that automatically sets the token (like the one above), 
# replace {{auth_token}} with the actual JWT token you received from logging in.
GET http://localhost:5000/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

### 5. Get All Students
GET http://localhost:5000/api/students
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

### 6. Test AI Chat Endpoint (Requires Gemini API Key in .env)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/ai/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

{
  "prompt": "Give me a 2 sentence summary of why AI is useful in education."
}
